n\nPlan:\n1. Call get_info('islurp') and get_info('LINEMODE') in parallel.\n2. Based on the source, write tests.\n\nLet me also think about what happens with `iter_by == 'LINEMODE'` when LINEMODE is None: `iter_by = LINEMODE` \u2192 None. Then `iter_by == LINEMODE` \u2192 True \u2192 fh.readline. Good.\n\nEdge: what if someone passes iter_by=0? functools.partial(fh.read, 0) \u2192 fh.read(0) returns '' immediately \u2192 EOF immediately \u2192 yields nothing. Not needed for coverage.\n\nNow, about the stdin test and NameError concern \u2014 let me wait for get_info results.\n\nAlso need to double check: does `pytutils.files` import cleanly? It imports functools, glob, os, sys. Fine.\n\nLet me also think about whether `from pytutils.files import islurp, LINEMODE` works \u2014 LINEMODE is a module-level constant. Yes.\n\nNow let me write the final test file (assuming stdin works \u2014 pending get_info):\n\n```python\nimport builtins\nimport io\nimport os\nimport sys\n\nimport pytest\n\nfrom pytutils.files import islurp, LINEMODE\n\n\ndef test_islurp_reads_lines_by_default(tmp_path):\n    path = tmp_path / \"lines.txt\"\n    path.write_text(\"first\\nsecond\\nthird\\n\")\n    assert list(islurp(str(path))) == [\"first\\n\", \"second\\n\", \"third\\n\"]\n\n\ndef test_islurp_accepts_linemode_string(tmp_path):\n    path = tmp_path / \"linemode.txt\"\n    path.write_text(\"alpha\\nbeta\\n\")\n    assert list(islurp(str(path), iter_by='LINEMODE')) == [\"alpha\\n\", \"beta\\n\"]\n\n\ndef test_islurp_reads_in_chunks(tmp_path):\n    path = tmp_path / \"chunks.txt\"\n    path.write_text(\"abcdefghij\")\n    assert list(islurp(str(path), iter_by=4)) == [\"abcd\", \"efgh\", \"ij\"]\n\n\ndef test_islurp_reads_stdin(monkeypatch):\n    fake_stdin = io.StringIO(\"stdin line 1\\nstdin line 2\\n\")\n    monkeypatch.setattr(sys, \"stdin\", fake_stdin)\n    assert list(islurp(\"-\")) == [\"stdin line 1\\n\", \"stdin line 2\\n\"]\n    assert not fake_stdin.closed  # stdin must not be clo